</TABLE> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">CCT&#146;s insurance transaction service customers accounted for 98.1% and 98.7% of the total accounts
receivable balance as of December 31, 2021 and 2022 respectively. These insurance transaction service customers are mainly group-wide insurance carrier conglomerates in China with a contractual and customary payment terms that generally range from
30 to 180 days. The accounts receivable that is more than 6 months old are mainly due from a branch of an insurance carrier conglomerate who operates in a province that had an extended period under a government mandated Covid-19 quarantine lock-down
measures, from August to December 2022. During the lock-down period for that province, no movements beyond the residential buildings were permitted. As a result, businesses and banks could not process normal scheduled payments. It was a unique
situation similar to a force majeure, rather than a credit default. In fact, these balances were substantially collected subsequent to the lock-down measures being lifted at the end of 2022. CCT determined that this balance was recoverable. As of
May 15, 2023, RMB323.4 million of CCT&#146;s accounts receivable as of December&nbsp;31, 2022 was subsequently collected by CCT. No amount of accounts receivable has been written off (i.e., charged-off against the allowance) for the periods
presented in the proxy statement/prospectus. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B><I>Accounts Payable </I></B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Accounts payable mainly includes payment to the cost of referral partners. Accounts payable increased by RMB46.9 million from RMB180.3 million
as of December 31, 2021 to RMB227.2 million as of December&nbsp;31, </P>
 <p STYLE="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&nbsp;</P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="center">251 </P>

</DIV></Center>


