<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman; " ALIGN="left">The total 760,000,000 Ordinary Shares to be issued as consideration for all outstanding CCT Ordinary Shares and
Preferred Shares include approximately 63,552 Class&nbsp;A Ordinary Shares underlying the assumed Innoven Warrant and 785,796 unvested Exchanged Restricted Shares. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<P STYLE="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Anticipated Accounting Treatment </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Under
both the no redemption and the maximum redemption scenarios, CCT was determined to be the accounting acquirer, and as such, the Business Combination will be treated as a reverse recapitalization in accordance with U.S. GAAP. Under this method of
accounting, Prime Impact will be treated as the &#147;acquired&#148; company for financial reporting purposes. Accordingly, the Business Combination will be treated as the equivalent of CCT issuing shares for the net assets of Prime Impact,
accompanied by a recapitalization. The net assets of Prime Impact will be stated at historical cost, with no goodwill or other intangible assets recorded. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The unaudited pro forma condensed combined financial information has been prepared using the assumptions below with respect to the potential
redemption into ordinary shares: </P> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
